# NodesModifier inputs: branch the dict write at 5.2

A Geometry Nodes modifier keeps its own copy of every input the node tree
exposes. Until 5.2 those values were ID properties on the modifier, keyed by
the socket identifier. Blender 5.2 replaced them with RNA properties:

| | 4.5 LTS | 5.1 | 5.2 LTS |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `mod[ident] = value` | works | works | `TypeError: bpy_struct[key] = val: id properties not supported for this type` |
| `getattr(mod.properties.inputs, ident).value = value` | `AttributeError: 'NodesModifier' object has no attribute 'properties'` | `AttributeError` | works |

No single form works everywhere, so this is one of the few writes that needs
a version branch. Branch at **5.2**, not 5.0: 5.1 still takes the dict form.

## What this rule flags

- `mod["Socket_<n>"] = ...`, `mod["Input_<n>"] = ...` or `mod[ident] = ...`
  on a `NODES` modifier with no `bpy.app.version` test around it
- A hard-coded identifier (`"Input_2"`, `"Socket_2"`): look it up from
  `tree.interface.items_tree` by name
- A branch at `(5, 0, 0)` for this write: it breaks 5.1

## Wrong

```python
mod = obj.modifiers.new(name="Displace", type='NODES')
mod.node_group = tree
mod["Socket_2"] = 2.5
```

On 5.2 the last line raises `TypeError`.

## Right

```python
import bpy

mod = obj.modifiers.new(name="Displace", type='NODES')
mod.node_group = tree
ident = next(item.identifier for item in tree.interface.items_tree
             if item.item_type == 'SOCKET' and item.in_out == 'INPUT'
             and item.name == "Strength")
if bpy.app.version >= (5, 2, 0):
    getattr(mod.properties.inputs, ident).value = 2.5
else:
    mod[ident] = 2.5
obj.update_tag()
bpy.context.view_layer.update()  # before evaluated_get reads the new value
```

## Verified

`examples/gn-modifier-inputs/` writes its inputs through this branch and
measures the evaluated extents on 4.5, 5.1 and 5.2. Its `--api dict`
falsifier exits 5 on 5.2 (the dict write raises) and `--api rna` exits 5 on
4.5 (no `properties`).

